  "title": "Warrior of Faith",
  "era": "conquest",
  "lifespan": "c. 1490–1370 BC",
  "summary": "Caleb was one of the twelve spies Moses sent to Canaan. Along with Joshua, he was the only one who believed that Israel could take possession of the land. As a reward, he and Joshua were the only ones of their generation allowed to enter the Promised Land. At the age of 85, he asked to be given the task of conquering Hebron.",
